 7. Nested Git Projects Issue
     Problem :- Adding existing Git repositories (`project_3`, `project_4`) into a parent repository may produce:
            create mode 160000 project_3
            create mode 160000 project_4

     Why It Happens
          1. Nested projects contain their own `.git` folders
          2. Git assumes you want submodules, not normal folders
          3. Adding directly triggers submodule tracking
 Solution: Convert Submodules to Normal Folders

 Step 1: Remove Inner `.git` Folders
          Remove-Item -Recurse -Force project_3\.git
          Remove-Item -Recurse -Force project_4\.git

 Step 2: Remove Git Index References
          git rm --cached project_3
          git rm --cached project_4

 Step 3: Add as Normal Folders
         git add project_3 project_4

 Step 4: Commit
        git commit -m "Convert nested projects to normal folders"

 Step 5: Push
      git push origin main

✅ Now `project_3` and `project_4` behave as normal folders, all files tracked, visible on GitHub.

