 8. Full Git Workflow Example for React Projects
    # Initialize repository
        git init
    
    # Stage files
        git add .
    
    # Commit changes
        git commit -m "Initial commit"
    
    # Add remote
        git remote add origin https://github.com/pradhan92/react-book.git
    
    # Push to main branch
        git push -u origin main


 Fix Nested Projects (project\_3 & project\_4)
    # Remove inner git folders
      Remove-Item -Recurse -Force project_3\.git, project_4\.git
    
    # Remove gitlinks
      git rm --cached project_3, project_4
    
    # Add as normal folders
      git add project_3 project_4
    
    # Commit & push
      git commit -m "Convert nested projects to normal folders"
      git push origin main


 9. all Git commands for creating a branch, making changes, pushing, and creating a pull request
    # 1. Check current branch
          git branch
    
    # 2. Create a new branch and switch to it
          git checkout -b feature-branch
    
    # 3. Make changes in your files (edit/add/delete)
    
    # 4. Stage all changes
          git add .
    
    # 5. Commit the changes
          git commit -m "Add new feature XYZ"
    
    # 6. Push the branch to GitHub and set upstream
          git push -u origin feature-branch
    
    # 7. On GitHub: create a Pull Request from 'feature-branch' to 'main'
    
    # 8. After PR is merged, switch back to main branch
          git checkout main
    
    # 9. Pull latest changes from remote main
          git pull origin main
    
    # 10. Optional: delete the local branch if done
          git branch -d feature-branch
    
    # 11. Optional: delete remote branch if done
          git push origin --delete feature-branch



 10. Common Git Errors & Fixes

| Error                          | Cause                    | Fix                                      |
| ------------------------------ | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |
| `create mode 160000 project_4` | Nested Git repo detected | Remove inner `.git` and re-add normally  |
| `! [rejected]` push            | Non-fast-forward         | `git pull --rebase` then `git push`      |
| LF → CRLF warning              | Windows line endings     | `git config --global core.autocrlf true` |


11. Tips & Best Practices

1. Avoid nested `.git` directories unless using submodules intentionally.
2. Use `.gitignore` for node\_modules, logs, env files.
3. Always commit small, meaningful changes.
4. Pull before pushing to avoid conflicts.
5. Use branches for features and merge into main when ready.
6. Keep commit messages clear and consistent.


